Q: odbc_connect(): SQL error: [unixODBC][Driver Manager]Data source name not found, and no default driver specified, SQL state IM002 in SQLConnect A: <p>If you're using FreeTDS, you need to specify the driver from <code>odbcinst.ini</code>, which is normally FreeTDS. Try:</p>

<pre><code>$DSN = 'UID=username;PWD=password;EngineName=dbServiceName;AutoStop=No;Integrated=No;Debug=No;DisableMultiRowFetch=No;CommLinks=SharedMemory,TCPIP{};Compress=No;Driver={FreeTDS}';
</code></pre>

Q: WPF combobox disabled background color A: <p>Depends on what you mean by &quot;not overrideable&quot;. This trigger in the template:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;Trigger Property=&quot;IsEnabled&quot; Value=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
    &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Foreground&quot; Value=&quot;{DynamicResource {x:Static SystemColors.GrayTextBrushKey}}&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Background&quot; Value=&quot;#FFF4F4F4&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/Trigger&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>It is what is setting the background. Thus, you have to override the template in order to customize it - there's no property on the control itself that is used to set the background when disabled, and there's no resource look up, so you can't alter it there either.</p>

Q: How to extract lines of text which do not start with an asterisk from a multi-line string A: <p>You can simply use</p>

<pre><code>^[^*]\S*
</code></pre>

<p>this and do a <code>match</code> instead of <code>split</code>.See demo.</p>

<p><a href="https://regex101.com/r/iV6mP5/2" rel="nofollow">https://regex101.com/r/iV6mP5/2</a></p>

<pre><code>$re = "/^[^*]\\S*/m"; 
$str = "abrakadabra\n* Eski çağlarda bazıhastalıklara iyi geldiğine inanılan büyülü söz\nabramaas\n* Abramak işi, idare.\nabradsma\n* Abramak işi, idare.\naswabrama\n* Abramak işi, idare."; 

preg_match_all($re, $str, $matches);
</code></pre>
